:: Silver Stranger Colosseum Return
<<effects>>
You stop beside them at the railing. They keep looking over the water while you explain what happened at the Colosseum.
<<if $xchange.colosseum.ending is "disrupted">>
	You tell them about the fighters behind the grey door, how you helped four of them leave through the delivery exit, and how the Colosseum banned you afterwards. They turn towards you when you mention the four fighters.
	<br><br>
	"Four?" they ask. "And now you want to go back?"
	<br><br>
	You explain that even after the date on the ban passes, the receptionist will no longer book you for another fight.
<<elseif $xchange.colosseum.ending is "walked" and $xchange.colosseum.banReason is "refused">>
	You tell them you turned down the crowd after a win, that the goons threw you out, and that the door has stayed shut since.
	<br><br>
	"You won and then said no." They seem to find that interesting. "The house takes that personally."
<<elseif $xchange.colosseum.ending is "walked">>
	You explain that you refused the championship offer and left the Colosseum. Since then, the receptionist has refused to put your name on another fight.
	<br><br>
	"You told them you were finished," they say. "I suppose they took you at your word."
<<else>>
	You tell them about the date beside your name on the banned list. You could wait until the ban ends, but you want to return before then.
	<br><br>
	"And you've come to me instead of waiting for the date to pass."
<</if>>
<br><br>
You ask whether they can speak to the Colosseum and get your name back on the fight list.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Colosseum Return]]>><</link>>

:: Silver Stranger Colosseum Return 2
<<effects>>
<<if !$xchange.silverStranger.colosseumReturns>>
	"Of course I can." They turn away from the water and rest one elbow on the railing. "But I'm always helping you, aren't I?"
	<br><br>
	You wait for them to continue. They study your face with a slight smile, making you wonder what they are about to ask for.
	<br><br>
	"What are you going to give me?"
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Offer money|Silver Stranger Colosseum Offer]]>><<set $phase to "money">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Offer items|Silver Stranger Colosseum Offer]]>><<set $phase to "items">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Offer anything|Silver Stranger Colosseum Offer]]>><<set $phase to "anything">><</link>>
<<else>>
	They look at you without smiling. "Again? I remember making that call for you. So will the person who answered it."
	<br><br>
	You start to explain, but they raise one hand and stop you. "A hundred thousand pounds. In cash."
	<br><br>
	You wait for them to laugh or lower the price, but they only lean back against the railing and watch you.
	<br><br>
	"You heard me. Take your time deciding."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Ask whether they even need money|Silver Stranger Colosseum Payment]]>><<set $phase to "question">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Consider the price|Silver Stranger Colosseum Payment]]>><<set $phase to "pay">><</link>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Drop the subject|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>

:: Silver Stranger Colosseum Offer
<<effects>>
<<switch $phase>>
	<<case "money">>
		You offer to pay for their help. Before you can name a price, they look at the pocket where you keep your money, then look back at you.
		<br><br>
		"Do I seem like someone who needs money?"
		<br><br>
		Your hand stops halfway to your pocket. They make no attempt to take anything from you.
		<br><br>
		"Try again. I'd like to hear what you think this is worth."
	<<case "items">>
		You suggest bringing them something instead. You could ask what they want, or offer something you already own.
		<br><br>
		"I see. I look like someone who's lacking something."
		<br><br>
		Their voice remains pleasant, but they remove their elbow from the railing and stand upright. You begin to explain what you meant, but they turn their head towards the path beside the docks instead of looking at you.
		<br><br>
		"I'm sure you chose that offer carefully."
		<br><br>
		You stop talking. They have not asked what you brought, and they show no interest in seeing it.
		<<npcincr Luchifen love -1>>| <span class="silverStranger">- ???</span>
	<<case "anything">>
		"Anything," you say.
		<br><br>
		"Anything?"
		<br><br>
		Their smile widens until you can see more of their teeth. You wait for them to laugh or tell you what they want, but they continue looking at you without speaking. You take one step backwards, and your feet hits a raised part of the paving. You stop and move your foot before you lose your balance.
		<<if $xchange.bankHeist?.heistComplete>>
			<br><br>
			The smile reminds you of the elk mask from the bank, with the same carved crescent shape across its face. You remember the red emergency light shining over it while Wren pulled you away and told you to stop looking.
			You swallow and look behind the Stranger, checking the open space near the docks even though nobody is standing there.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		They notice you looking around, then look at you again. They stop showing their teeth, leaving only a small smile.
		"Let's start with having you back in the pit. I dislike going there and finding nothing worth watching."
		<br><br>
		"That's all?" you ask.
		<br><br>
		"That's what I'm asking for." They wait while you think about it. "And you'll be listed as Knife. Whatever name you've made for yourself, that's what they'll put on the board."
		<br><br>
		They move one hand towards their coat pocket, then stop before reaching inside. "Still want my help?"
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<if $phase is "anything">>
	<<link [[Accept their help|Silver Stranger Colosseum Restored]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Offer anything|Silver Stranger Colosseum Offer]]>><<set $phase to "anything">><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Colosseum Payment
<<effects>>
<<if $phase is "question">>
	"Do you even need money?" you ask.
	<br><br>
	They shrug. "No. That doesn't stop me asking for it."
	<br><br>
	They wait until you look back at them before continuing. "You want me to make the same call again. I want you to think about how often you're going to ask."
<<else>>
	You repeat the amount to make sure you heard it correctly. They nod immediately.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"A hundred thousand pounds, and you go back on the board as Knife. You know how this works by now."
They take out their phone and hold it in one hand without unlocking it. They wait for your answer before doing anything else.
<br><br>
<<if $money gte 10000000>>
	<<link [[Pay £100,000 in cash|Silver Stranger Colosseum Restored]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<span class="red">You need £100,000 in cash.</span>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Decline|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>

:: Silver Stranger Colosseum Restored
<<effects>>
<<if $xchange.colosseum?.joined gte 1 and ($xchange.colosseum.banUntil gt Time.date.timeStamp or ["walked", "disrupted"].includes($xchange.colosseum.ending)) and (!$xchange.silverStranger.colosseumReturns or $money gte 10000000)>>
	<<if $xchange.silverStranger.colosseumReturns>>
		<<money -10000000 "silverStrangerFavor" {cashOnly: true}>>
		You hand over the money. They check each bundle, counting through the notes while you stand beside them. When they finish, they put the money away.
		"Now we can get on with it."
	<<else>>
		You tell them to make the call. They take their phone from their coat but keep looking at you, waiting to see whether you change your mind.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	They dial a number and hold the phone to their ear. Someone answers, but the wind covers most of what they say.
	"Put Knife back on the card."
	<br><br>
	The person on the other end speaks for several seconds. The Stranger turns towards the water and waits until they finish.
	<br><br>
	"Yes. I know what happened. I was quite clear about what I wanted."
	<<if $xchange.colosseum.ending is "disrupted" and $xchange.colosseum.debt is 0>>
		They look back at you. "And call off the people you've sent after this one. You can fill your own rooms."
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	The next reply is shorter. The Stranger ends the call and puts the phone back into their coat.
	<br><br>
	<<set $xchange.silverStranger.colosseumReturns to ($xchange.silverStranger.colosseumReturns ?? 0) + 1>>
	<<set $xchange.colosseum.callbacks.silver to 1>>
	<<set $xchange.colosseum.banUntil to 0>>
	<<if ["walked", "disrupted"].includes($xchange.colosseum.ending)>>
		<<set $xchange.colosseum.ending to "">><<unset $xchange.colosseum.banReason>>
		<<if $xchange.colosseum.debt is 0>>
			<<set $xchange.colosseum.hunt to 0>><<set $xchange.colosseum.huntUntil to 0>><<set $xchange.colosseum.huntWins to 0>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<set $xchange.colosseum.arenaName to "Knife">>
	"There. Try not to get yourself banned again before I see you fight."
	<<if $xchange.colosseum.debt gt 0>>
		<br><br>
		Before you can thank them, they add, "You still owe them money. This doesn't settle that account, or stop them collecting it."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">The Colosseum has lifted your ban and will book you again.</span> <span class="purple">Your arena name is now Knife.</span> You still need to meet the usual fighting requirements.
<<else>>
	They put their phone away without calling. "We haven't got a deal to settle."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>

:: Underground Colosseum Silver Return
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<colosseumHost>>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.callbacks.silver to 0>>
The receptionist sees you approaching the fighters' desk and waves you over. <<He>> reaches under the ledger, takes out a booking slip, and places it on the desk.
Your rank is correct, but <span class="pink">Knife</span> is written across the top in fresh ink.
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.silverStranger.colosseumReturns is 1>>
	"Got a phone call about you." <<He>> picks up a slip from the desk. "You're allowed to fight here again."
	You reach for it, but <<he>> does not let go yet. "You're still following our rules. Whoever called doesn't change that."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> points to the name written at the top. "And this is the name you're using."
	<br><br>
	The Stranger walks up beside you. As soon as the receptionist sees them, <<he>> lets go of the slip.
	"Of course," they says. "The usual rules are fine."
	<br><br>
	The receptionist looks down at the ledger and starts writing your details without asking anything else.
	<br><br>
	The Stranger takes the slip from your hand and looks at the name. "Anything, you said." They hand it back. "When you're ready, give me a fight worth watching."
	<br><br>
	They look towards the pit, where an attendant is preparing the sand for the next fight.
	"You don't need to win for me," they add. "Just focus on the fight."
	<br><br>
	The Stranger heads towards the gallery and climbs the stairs. Once they are gone, the receptionist points at the slip in your hand.
	"Keep that with you. If anyone says you shouldn't be here, send them to me."
<<else>>
	"Knife. Again." <<He>> pushes the slip across the desk. "The call came through. You're allowed to fight again."
	<br><br>
	You ask if there is anything else you need to do. <<He>> checks the ledger.
	<<if $xchange.colosseum.debt gt 0>>
		"You still owe us money. That hasn't changed."
	<<else>>
		"No. Just show that slip when you book a fight."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	The Stranger is standing near the gallery stairs. They notice the slip in your hand and raise an eyebrow.
	"Try not to lose this one," they say. "You're making them write your name often enough already."
	<br><br>
	You hold onto the slip as the Stranger turns away and walks up the gallery stairs.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Enter the Colosseum|Underground Colosseum]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
